# Template for /etc/jobbliggaren/detection.env — gate M-7 (#1201).
#
# Install as root:
#   sudo install -d -m 0700 -o root -g root /etc/jobbliggaren
#   sudo install -m 0600 -o root -g root <this file> /etc/jobbliggaren/detection.env
#   sudo nano /etc/jobbliggaren/detection.env        # paste the real URL
#
# THE REAL FILE IS NEVER COMMITTED. Only this template is, and the template holds no value.
#
# WHY THIS LIVES ON PERSISTENT DISK AND NOT IN THE tmpfs SECRETS DIRECTORY. /run/jobbliggaren is
# RAM-backed and empty after every reboot. Put the URL there and the heartbeat goes silent on
# every restart until an operator injects — producing a dead-man page with NO diagnosis, instead
# of a `/fail` page that names the real condition. A persistent file means that after an
# unplanned reboot the heartbeat keeps reporting and says what is actually wrong.
#
# WHAT THIS VALUE IS. A capability URL: possession is authority, there is no second factor. It is
# 0600 root:root, never logged, never echoed by the script, and never included in any diagnostic.
# It is also passed to curl ON STDIN (`--config -`) rather than as an argument, because an
# argument is world-readable in /proc/<pid>/cmdline for the life of the process — "not logged" is
# not the same as "not exposed", and the argv path was the one place it still was.
#
# WHAT A STOLEN COPY BUYS AN ATTACKER, stated rather than left to be discovered: the ability to
# suppress or forge this box's alarms. A root attacker can already do that by leaving the
# heartbeat running, so the credential grants no capability the threat model (ADR 0123) did not
# already concede. That is exactly why this channel shape was chosen over one whose credential
# would open a SECOND failure domain — a log-sink token, an AWS key, or a repository PAT.

# The expecter's ping endpoint. The script POSTs here on success, and to <url>/fail with an
# allowlisted diagnosis when a predicate is false. Silence past the expecter's grace period is
# the dead-man alarm.
HEARTBEAT_PING_URL=https://hc-ping.com/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
